# Autoform CODEOWNERS example. GitHub does not read this filename.
#
# Copy these rules into the first CODEOWNERS file GitHub reads:
#   .github/CODEOWNERS, CODEOWNERS, or docs/CODEOWNERS
# If none exists, use .github/CODEOWNERS. Replace @OWNER with GitHub users or
# visible teams that have write access, then uncomment the rules.
#
# The roadmap rule protects open_statements, which decides whether a theorem
# may merge with a sorry proof. The .github rule protects Autoform's workflows
# and audit script. Consider rules for lakefile.toml or lakefile.lean,
# lean-toolchain, and lake-manifest.json too; they decide what CI compiles.
#
# GitHub reads CODEOWNERS from a pull request's base branch. New rules cannot
# protect their own activation unless equivalent coverage already exists
# there, so review that change explicitly. Then require pull requests and
# code-owner review, dismiss stale approvals, and audit every bypass.

# /blueprint/roadmap/README.md @OWNER
# /.github/ @OWNER
